    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Coral adaptation to climate change",
    "problem": "The lack of direct evidence for corals' adaptive responses to climate change, such as shifting to more thermally tolerant algal symbionts, hinders the ability to predict the long-term survival of reefs facing increased bleaching events.",
    "method": "The paper proposes that an adaptive shift in coral symbiont communities toward more thermally tolerant types is a natural mechanism that allows devastated reefs to become more resistant to future bleaching caused by climate change.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate whether severe coral bleaching events can drive an adaptive shift in coral populations towards hosting more thermally tolerant algal symbionts, thereby increasing the resilience of reefs to future climate change.",
